  "final_text": "I fixed the bug in `invoicing/currency.py`, and the full test suite now passes (8 tests).\n\n**Cause:** `minor_units()` changed the currency code to lowercase (`\"jpy\"`) before looking it up in `ZERO_DECIMAL`, but that set holds uppercase codes (`{\"JPY\", \"KRW\"}`). The lookup never matched, so yen was treated as having 2 decimal places. That made the amount 100\u00d7 too large, and it printed as `\u00a514,118.50` instead of `\u00a514,118`.\n\n**Change:** `currency.lower()` is now `currency.upper()`, so currency codes match the set whatever their case."
